SUPPLY CHAIN MORNING
Issue 316 | Friday, March 20, 2026

Good morning. Friday, so a short one and the weekly rate table.

1) Oakland's first Saturday gate is tomorrow
Truckers have booked about 600 appointments for the 7am-3pm window, which the terminal called "encouraging." Central Valley ag exporters are the target; if the first month works, the port has said it will make the Saturday gate permanent through October.

2) Fertilizer: urea up 18% in three weeks
A combination of natural-gas prices in Europe, an export restriction in a major producing country, and the spring application window arriving early. Growers who did not pre-buy are paying up. Barge traffic on the upper Mississippi is running two weeks early because of the mild winter, which helps.

3) The week in rates
Transpacific spot: $1,905/FEU, flat. Dry van spot: $2.19/mile ex-fuel, up 5 cents. Diesel: $4.06, up 4 cents. Air, Hong Kong-Chicago: $4.10/kg, down 3%. Warehouse asking rents, national: flat.

NUMBER OF THE DAY: 2.4 million. Stone-fruit cartons forecast to ship from the southern Central Valley in the next six weeks, the earliest start to the season in a decade. Reefer capacity out of Fresno and Oakland is already tight.

Have a good weekend.

